fs: detached mounts series from 6.15, adapted to 6.12

Backport of upstream's "fs: allow detached mounts" work (Christian Brauner,
v6.15), so open_tree(OPEN_TREE_CLONE) works on a detached mount: Talos
v1.14's machined binds its /etc overlay read-only that way and exits at
boot with EINVAL without it.

Upstream commits, in order:
  3b0cdba4da55 fs: record sequence number of origin mount namespace
  2f576220cd81 fs: add mnt_ns_empty() helper
  043bc81efbfc fs: add assert for move_mount()
  b73ec10a4587 fs: add fastpath for dissolve_on_fput()
  9ed72af4e292 fs: add may_copy_tree()
  c5c12f871a30 fs: create detached mounts from detached mounts
  21107723831e fs: mount detached mounts onto detached mounts
  f8b6cd66e479 fs: allow creating detached mounts from fsmount() file descriptors
  064fe6e233e8 mount: handle mount propagation for detached mount trees

Adaptations for 6.12:
  - seq_origin is added beside seq in struct mnt_namespace (the context
    differs).
  - VFS_WARN_ON_ONCE() is defined as WARN_ON_ONCE() in fs/mount.h when the
    tree does not have it.
  - may_copy_tree() checks nsfs only: pidfs bind-mounts arrived in 6.13.
  - may_use_mount() is placed before do_move_mount() (the context differs).
  - f9fde814de37 (getname_maybe_null() in move_mount()) and its fix
    99b6a1dee086 are left out: 6.12 has no getname_maybe_null(), and Talos
    passes an empty path with MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH, which 6.12 handles.

